# Sergei's tomb (K85), in castle_ravenloft_catacombs_tombs (docs/regions/castle_ravenloft_catacombs.md §3, §6).
# sarcophagus: the prop cat_sergei_sarcophagus; take_treasure is the Tarokka spot for castle_ravenloft_sergeis_tomb.
# font: the basin of still water at the tomb's foot (cat_sergei_font). Sergei is seen only in still water, and only
# beside Ireena; her scene plays once, from either prop, when she travels with the party.

~ sarcophagus
if guest:ireena and not flag.cat_ireena_at_tomb
-> ireena_arrives
endif
-> tomb_look

~ tomb_look
Narrator: A long sarcophagus of white stone. On the lid a young man lies at rest in an old-fashioned coat, a sunburst on his breast and his hands folded on the hilt of a sword. Someone has kept the stone clean.
if treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_sergeis_tomb
Narrator: Between the stone hands, laid across the sunburst, is something that was never carved.
endif
-> tomb_menu

~ tomb_menu
* [if treasure_at:castle_ravenloft_sergeis_tomb] Take what lies in his hands. -> take_treasure
* Read the words on the lid. -> inscription
* [if not flag.cat_sergei_rites_said] [Religion DC 13] Say the rites for the dead over him. -> rites | rites_lost
* Leave him in peace. -> END

~ take_treasure
Narrator: It comes away easily, as if the hands had only been holding it until somebody asked.
tarokka give castle_ravenloft_sergeis_tomb
interject tag:pious: He kept it for us. Four hundred years in the ground and still on the right side.
-> tomb_menu

~ inscription
Narrator: SERGEI VON ZAROVICH, and under the name, smaller: BELOVED. Under that, scratched much later by a less steady hand: FORGIVE ME.
interject tag:curious: That last line isn't the mason's. Somebody came down here with a knife and did it himself.
interject class:wizard: One can guess who. One would rather not.
-> tomb_menu

~ rites
set cat_sergei_rites_said
Narrator: The old words, said properly, in a room that has heard only one man's apologies for a very long time. The candle flames lean toward the tomb, and then stand up straight again.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You said the rites over Sergei's tomb
-> tomb_menu

~ rites_lost
set cat_sergei_rites_said
Narrator: The words come out in the wrong order, the way they do at a stranger's grave. Nothing answers. Nothing seems to mind, either.
-> tomb_menu

~ font
if guest:ireena and not flag.cat_ireena_at_tomb
-> ireena_arrives
endif
Narrator: A round basin cut into the floor at the foot of the tomb, filled to the brim with water so still it looks like a sheet of black glass.
if flag.cat_ireena_at_tomb
Narrator: Since Ireena knelt here, there is a little light low down in the water, like a coal under ash.
endif
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ireena

~ ireena_arrives
cutscene sergei_font
Narrator: Ireena stops in the doorway. She reads the name on the lid, and then she walks past it without a word and kneels by the basin at its foot.
if flag.ireena_pool_vision
-> ireena_knows
endif
-> ireena_first_sight

~ ireena_first_sight
set cat_ireena_at_tomb = "remembered"
Narrator: In the still water, beside her reflection, there is a second face: a young man with kind eyes and a sunburst at his throat. You look up. Nobody kneels beside her.
Sergei von Zarovich: Tatyana.
Ireena [afraid]: No. My name is Ireena.
Sergei von Zarovich: Not this time. I know. Forgive me. I only ever had the one name for you.
Ireena: You're the brother. The one on the lid. I've dreamed your face for years and never known whose it was.
Sergei von Zarovich: There is a pool at the top of the valley where the sun stays in the water. I can say more there. Here I am mostly bones.
if flag.eva_recognized_ireena
interject tag:curious: Madam Eva said she'd come round again. I thought it was the sort of thing fortune-tellers say.
endif
* Ask her what she wants to do. -> ireena_wants
* (Wait. Let her have this.) -> ireena_fade

~ ireena_wants
Ireena: First, he dies. The one upstairs. After that I'll find that pool, and I'll decide there. Not in a cellar, with all of you watching.
-> ireena_fade

~ ireena_knows
if flag.ireena_pool_choice == "promised"
-> ireena_promised
endif
-> ireena_farewell

~ ireena_promised
set cat_ireena_at_tomb = "promised"
Narrator: The water shivers and settles, and he is there beside her, the way he was at the pool.
Sergei von Zarovich: You came the long way round.
Ireena: I said I'd come back to you when he's dead. I'm close now. He's somewhere under our feet.
Sergei von Zarovich: I know where he is. I have always known where he is.
Ireena: Then wait a little longer.
Sergei von Zarovich: I have had practice.
-> ireena_fade

~ ireena_farewell
set cat_ireena_at_tomb = "farewell"
Narrator: The water shivers and settles, and he is there beside her.
Ireena: I said goodbye to you at the pool. I'm saying it again here, to your bones, so that it's done properly. Father would want it done properly.
Narrator: She takes the ribbon out of her hair and lays it on the lid, over the stone sunburst.
Sergei von Zarovich: Go and live, Ireena.
Ireena [sad]: That's the first time you've called me that.
-> ireena_fade

~ ireena_fade
Narrator: The second face is gone. The water is only water, and Ireena gets up off her knees and brushes the dust from them, and is herself again, mostly.
interject guest:ireena: Don't. Whatever it is. Later, when we're out in the air.
approve wren_featherfoot +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You let Ireena have her moment at Sergei's tomb
-> tomb_look
